  "source_review": [
    {
      "area": "Minimal production change",
      "finding": "Each file adds exactly one read-only fixed_run conjunction: F407 RCC->APB1LPENR & RCC_APB1LPENR_TIM2LPEN; GD RCU_APB1SPEN & RCU_APB1SPEN_TIMER1SPEN must be nonzero. Removing it restores each whole baseline file exactly. No clock repair, register write, initialization, owner state, ABI, namespace or dynamic path added."
    },
    {
      "area": "Selected physical gate",
      "finding": "Vendor headers place both selected sleep-enable registers at offset0x60, TIM2/TIMER1 bit0. Existing family timebase_lowpower admission checks these same gates. This check establishes sleep-gate admission only, not all timer configuration/health/wake IRQ/clock ownership."
    },
    {
      "area": "Final masked observation",
      "finding": "Original context/mask validation and IRQ save remain. Actual fixed_run MMIO read occurs under the saved mask after closed-domain quiescence and before acquire wake-sequence load/WFI. Removing an initially enabled bit in the IRQ-save hook is rejected by that actual later read. No cached gate or duplicate pre-mask check claim."
    },
    {
      "area": "Failure contract",
      "finding": "For valid shallow-sleep input and quiescent closed domain, missing gate yields NX_ERROR_UNSUPPORTED, slept=false, no WFI, restored IRQ state. Existing invalid/context/BUSY/barrier precedence remains. No token revocation, barrier consumption, domain/sequence mutation, reset or clock repair."
    },
    {
      "area": "Regression mechanism",
      "finding": "Two new cases use actual production sleep providers plus existing real clock-domain and guarded-WFI model; only CPU/context boundary leaves are injected. Missing-at-call and removed-at-final-mask each check unsupported/false/no WFI/restored mask, exact8192 MMIO bytes, domain/barrier/token bytes and wake sequence. Restoring the bit by external owner permits sleep on the same retained barrier."
    },
    {
      "area": "Preserved tests",
      "finding": "All18 old unique TEST_F bodies exact (17 F407 and18 GD runtime cases, one GD-only). Fixture explicitly enables the newly required gate. Existing context/deep/dynamic/wake/source/domain/borrow/overlap assertions remain. No filter/shard/skip/framework/debt change."
    },
    {
      "area": "Scope limit",
      "finding": "Shallow-sleep admission correction only. No claim of complete timer configuration, dynamic clocks, Stop continuity, active-I/O enrollment beyond contract, IO30 completion, current linked ARM budget, clean installed SDK, offline dual-build candidate or physical MCU/HIL."
    }
  ],
